      "text": "To find the simplified value of the fourth term of the given sequence, we first need to understand the sequence itself. The sequence is defined as the sum of consecutive powers of 3. The general form of the \\(n\\)-th term in the sequence can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ a_n = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + \\cdots + 3^{n-1} \\]\n\nThis is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common ratio \\(r = 3\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[ S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1} \\]\n\nFor our sequence, we need to find the fourth term (\\(a_4\\)), so we substitute \\(n = 4\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(r = 3\\) into the formula:\n\n\\[ a_4 = 1 \\frac{3^4 - 1}{3 - 1} = \\frac{3^4 - 1}{2} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(3^4\\):\n\n\\[ 3^4 = 81 \\]\n\nSo, the expression for the fourth term becomes:\n\n\\[ a_4 = \\frac{81 - 1}{2} = \\frac{80}{2} = 40 \\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of the fourth term of the sequence is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{40} \\]",
